From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 04:02:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Run no user APC in NtCancelIoFile().

The completion APCs of what is cancelled run at the next alertable wait,
as ntdll's pipe test checks.  With the wait for the cancellation
alertable, a user APC queued meanwhile ended NtCancelIoFile() with
STATUS_USER_APC, possibly before the cancellation was done.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
index 5e78e1ad581..4ec5cc14b4e 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/file.c
@@ -7290,7 +7290,8 @@ static NTSTATUS cancel_io( HANDLE handle, IO_STATUS_BLOCK *io, IO_STATUS_BLOCK *
 
     if (!status && cancel_handle)
     {
-        NtWaitForSingleObject( cancel_handle, TRUE, NULL );
+        /* the completion APCs of what is cancelled run at the next alertable wait, not in here */
+        NtWaitForSingleObject( cancel_handle, FALSE, NULL );
         NtClose( cancel_handle );
     }
     else if (status == STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE)
